{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"113272","commit":"f93cf80dc1d131dbaf65ea1876f76c908bf3c65b","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"In the `makeSupplier` method, when handling single elements, the code directly returns the element as a double value. This approach can lead to precision issues if the original type was an integer or long and the value is outside the range of what can be accurately represented by a double. Consider using a more precise type conversion or documenting this behavior.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/AvgTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/AvgTests.java-2845:3748-2826:2872,2904:2908,2923:3962","promptId":"#54Y24","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/AvgTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/AvgTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2845,"endPos":3748,"startLine":68,"startLineOffset":30,"endLine":85,"endLineOffset":13,"length":904}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2826,"endPos":2872,"startLine":67,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":67,"endLineOffset":58,"length":47},{"pos":2904,"endPos":2908,"startLine":69,"startLineOffset":30,"endLine":69,"endLineOffset":34,"length":5},{"pos":2923,"endPos":3962,"startLine":71,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":87,"endLineOffset":13,"length":1040}]}]},{"comment":"The `addSuppliers` method introduces a new way of adding suppliers to the cases list. However, it does not handle the case where `minRows` is greater than 1 and less than or equal to `maxRows`. This could lead to missing test cases for scenarios where more than one row but fewer than the maximum number of rows are required. The method should be adjusted to ensure that all valid ranges between `minRows` and `maxRows` are covered.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java